# Shell scripts are executed under WSL/Linux even when checked out on Windows.
# With core.autocrlf=true git would rewrite them to CRLF in the working tree,
# and bash fails on the trailing CR ("set: pipefail: invalid option name", or a
# syntax error at whatever line it reaches first). Pin them to LF regardless of
# the user's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for tool scripts invoked with a shebang.
*.py text eol=lf
